==Lithuanian==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|lt|h₃emh₃}}
Attestations with the meaning “power, consciousness” support a connection with {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|अम||tr=áma-|strength}}, {{etyl|ae|-}} {{m|ae|𐬇𐬨𐬀||attacking power, strength, potence}}<ref>Rolandas Kregždys ('''2002''') [http://www.baltistica.lt/index.php/baltistica/article/download/721/660 Dėl lie. ãmas] [Concerning lit. ãmas]. ''Baltistica'', volume 37, number 2, pages 269-272</ref>; From {{etyl|ine-pro|-}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃emh₃-||take hold of; be strong}}. This root has been connected with {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|ὄμνυμι||swear}}, {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|अमन्ति||tr=amánti|take hold of, swear}}, and most likely {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|amō||love}}.<ref>{{R:ine:deVaan2008}}</ref>

Must be separated from {{m|lt|ãmalioti||talk nonsense}}, of [[onomatopoeia|onomatopoeic]] origin. See {{m|lt|am̃sėti||yap, yelp}}.

===Noun===
{{lt-noun|head=ãmas|m|amaĩ|4}}

# {{lb|lt|Western Aukštaitian}} [[speech]], [[voice]]

